racasei K56 on body fat and metabolic parameters in adult individuals with obesity: a pilot study Guzailinuer Kadeer1, Wanrui Fu1, Yaqi He1, Ying Feng1*, Wei‑Hsein Liu2, Wei‑Lian Hung2*, Haotian Feng2 and Wen Zhao2 Abstract Background Studies || The purpose of this study was to evaluate the effect of a novel probiotic strain Lacticaseibacillus paracasei K56 on body fat and metabolic biomarkers in adult individuals with obesity. || Methods 74 adult subjects with obesity (body mass index ≥ 30 kg/m2, or percent body fat > 25% for men, percent body fat > 30% for women) were randomized into 5 groups and supplemented with different doses of K56 (groups VL_K56, L_K56, H_K56, and VH_K56: K56 capsules, 2 × 107 CFU/day, 2 × 109 CFU/day, 2 × 1010 CFU/day, 2 × 1011 CFU/ day, respectively) or placebo (group Pla: plac || Results The results showed that the L_K56 group had significant decreases in percent body fat (p = 0.004), visceral fat area (p = 0.0007), total body fat mass (p = 0.018), trunk body fat mass (p = 0.003), waist circumference (p = 0.003), gly‑ cosylated hemoglobin(p = 0.002) at the end of the study compared with baseline. || There were non‑significant reduc‑ tions in Body weight and BMI in the L_K56, H_K56, VL_K56 groups, whereas increases were observed in the placebo and VH_K56 groups compared with baseline values. || In addition, K56 supplementation modulated gut microbiota characteristics and diversity indices in the L‑K56 group. || Conclusions The results suggest that supplementation with different doses of Lacticaseibacillus paracasei K56 has certain effect on reducing body fat and glycosylated hemoglobin, especially at a dose of 109 CFU/day.","Kadeer et al. Nutrition & Metabolism (2023) 20:16 https://doi.org/10.1186/s12986-023-00739-y RESEARCH Effect of different doses of Lacticaseibacillus paracasei K56 on body fat and metabolic parameters in adult individuals with obesity: a pilot study Guzailinuer Kadeer1, Wanrui Fu1, Yaqi He1, Ying Feng1*, Wei‑Hsein Liu2