l fat mass reported a signi ﬁcant reduction in these variables. || Characteristics of the studies Reduction P a Signiﬁcant Non signi ﬁcant Body Weight (kg) Duration of the study (weeks) /C21 12 (n ¼ 18) 9 (50%) 9 (50%) 0.007 <12 (n ¼ 10) 0 (0%) 10 (100%) Dose of probiotics (CFU/day) /C21 1010 (n ¼ 19) 7 (37%) 12 (63%) 0.477 < 1010 (n ¼ 5) 1 (20%) 4 (80%) Vehicle of probiotic Capsule/Powder (n ¼ 15) 7 (47%) 8 (53%) 0.030 Dairy (n ¼ 12) 1 (8%) 11 (92%) Energy restriction Yes (n ¼ 9) 1 (11%) 8 (89%) 0.136 No (n ¼ 18) 7 (39%) 11 (61%) Number of species /C21 2( n ¼ 15) 4 (27%) 11 (73%) || Characteristics of the studies Reduction Pa Signﬁcant Non signi ﬁcant Body Weight (kg) Duration of the study and dose of probiotics <12 weeks and < 1010 CFU/day (n ¼ 3) 0 (0%) 3 (100%) 0.112 <12 weeks and /C21 1010 CFU/day (n ¼ 5) 0 (0%) 5 (100%) /C21 12 weeks and < 1010 CFU/day (n ¼ 2) 1 (50%) 1 (50%) /C21 12 weeks and /C21 1010 CFU/day (n ¼ 14) 7 (50%) 7 (50%) Body Mass index (kg/m 2) Duration of the study and dose of probiotics <12 weeks and < 1010 CFU/day (n ¼ 4) 0 (0%) 4 (100%) 0.302 <12 weeks and /C21 1010 CF || Characteristics of the studies Reduction Pa Signiﬁcant Non signi ﬁcant Body Weight (kg) Duration of the study and vehicle of probiotics <12 weeks and dairy (n ¼ 7) 0 (0%) 7 (100%) 0.027 <12 weeks and capsule/sachet/powder (n ¼ 3) 0 (0%) 3 (100%) /C21 12 weeks and dairy (n ¼ 5) 1 (20%) 4 (80%) /C21 12 weeks and capsule/sachet/powder (n ¼ 12) 7 (58%) 5 (42%) Body Mass index (kg/m 2) Duration of the study and vehicle of probiotics <12 weeks and dairy (n ¼ 7) 2 (29%) 5 (71%) 0.044 <12 weeks and capsule/sachet/powder (n","In gut dysbiosis, suppression of the AMPK occurs, leading to less oxidation of fatty acids and an increase in triglyceride synthesis [67,71]. || 95% CI: /C0 0.30, /C0 0.13, p < 0.001), and waist circumference (/C0 0.60 cm; || P < 0.0001) and body adiposity in individuals with overweight and obesity [25], but the results of the different studies were controvers