ease of L-Ruminococcuscould also be explained by probiotic administration[50 || increase in Butyricicoccus often associated with the low-fat diets [51 || increase in dietary ﬁber intake could be related to the signi ﬁca- tive decrease of Eubacterium at T2 || change [60","Applied nutritional investigation Gut microbiota composition after diet and probiotics in overweight breast cancer survivors: a randomized open-label pilot intervention trial Marianna Pellegrini M.D. a, Mirko Ippolito M.D. a, Taira Monge R.D. a, Rossella Violi R.D. a, Paola Cappello M.D. b, Ilario Ferrocino Ph.D. c, Luca Simone Cocolin Ph.D. c, Antonella De Francesco M.D. a, Simona Bo Ph.D. d, Concetta Finocchiaro Ph",diet || intervention || control || probiotic || exercise || Akkermansia,12 g || 0.001 G,8 wk,n = 16 || n = 18 || 34 participants || n = 12 || n = 14,ok,
